{
  "helped": [
    "inputs/brief.md lines 3-4 gave the exact `npx --no-install gennady sdd-new module --scope token --module pipeline/normalize` invocation; its manifest returned spec-id, NOR acronym, and relative link forms (call_00_6YPkIhYkMXIvpdDSueCr3521).",
    "ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml STEP_2_FILL mandated one whole-file Write replacing the skeleton and forbade Edit/Patch; followed in call_00_AucSM2eH8r6sitZRvPhD0261.",
    "ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/module-spec-structure.xml supplied section order and FOLD rules; entity-inventory-format.xml, entity-surface-format.xml, and dbc-contracts.xml were readable lazily at their owning sections (call_01_1nYWS5`…`, call_02_diNGD…, call_03_sXUmg…).",
    "The brief's terminal step plus module.directive.xml STEP_4_CHECK matched; `sdd-check --spec … --authoring` returned clean (call_00_r82Fuw9ryDuOpgcrAGdg3178)."
  ],
  "friction": [
    "requirement-entry-format.xml (Trigger/Modality) vs the parent TOK-REQ-1 wording: it was unclear whether a module requirement may restate/narrow the parent's allowed-character contract or must only add a narrower obligation. I chose to restate; host reports semanticVerdict=fail, so this is a plausible but unconfirmed cause.",
    "module-spec-structure.xml HANDOFF template lists implementation/test files, stack, rules, risks only; the task demanded pending approval. I added `Status: pending-operator` and `Operator decision: pending` keys not present in the template. Whether those extra keys are permitted or count as semantic drift is unknown."
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "Cause of semanticVerdict=fail is unknown; I did not receive a semantic finding, so I will not assign one.",
    "Whether the two extra Input/Outcome rows (separator-only, non-ASCII) beyond the two required rows are acceptable is unknown.",
    "The target language is not named in brief.md or token.spec.md; I inferred TypeScript from package.json `type: module`. The template's MODULE_USAGE_EXAMPLE requires a target-language snippet but no source fixes the language.",
    "Whether a single-entity module should still draw a Call Chain is ambiguous: dbc-contracts.xml CALL_CHAIN_FORMAT's floor applies below the ≥2-abstraction threshold, which I stated explicitly, but the floor wording refers mainly to the dependency graph."
  ],
  "nextHypothesis": {
    "avoidableAction": "The broad `ls -la && find specs ai -maxdepth 4 … | head -100` (call_00_UOg6porhp3dOsmM6RnpH4652) was avoidable; reading token.spec.md and specs/README.md alone would have oriented the route. Similarly the `rg` lookup for format anchors (call_00_w5rQlUDOcLdMY4t5t7EU0799) overlapped with the direct format reads that followed.",
    "instructionChangeToTest": "Add one sentence to module-spec-structure.xml MODULE_REQUIREMENTS or requirement-entry-format.xml: a module requirement may not redefine the parent's input contract; it must cite the parent ID and state only the narrower delta. Test whether that removes the semantic failure without changing the module's observable behavior.",
    "secondaryTest": "State in module-spec-structure.xml HANDOFF whether approval-boundary keys (`Status`, `Operator decision`) belong in this section or only in the scope HANDOFF."
  }
}
